{"id":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--sequence-of-rokkoka-and-anan","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topics":["topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--double-evidentiality"],"statement":{"en":"The auxiliary anan can immediately follow rok'oka in sequence.","ja":"rok'oka の直後にさらに anan が後続することがある。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["rok'oka","anan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0096-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--horobetsu-evidentials-grammaticalized-as-clause-markers","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topics":["topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--grammaticalization-cline"],"statement":{"en":"In the Horobetsu dialect, evidential markers have grammaticalized into forms that independently introduce adverbial clauses.","ja":"幌別方言において、証拠性形式は単独で副詞節を形成するマーカーへと文法化している。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0004-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--aan-rokkoka-admirative-mood-auxiliaries","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topics":["topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--mirativity-aan"],"statement":{"en":"The admirative mood auxiliary is aan for singular subjects and rok'oká for plural subjects.","ja":"感嘆法（ミラティヴ）補助動詞は単数主語に対して aan、複数主語に対して rok'oká である。"},"type":"paradigm-cell","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["aan","rok'oká"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0018-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--chitose-anan-corresponds-to-saru-aan","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topics":["topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--mirativity-aan"],"statement":{"en":"In Chitose Ainu, the admirative mood auxiliary corresponding to Saru aan is an'an.","ja":"千歳アイヌ語において、沙流方言の aan に対応する感嘆法補助動詞は an'an である。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["an'an","aan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0018-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--aan-rokkoka-admirative-mood-auxiliaries","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Identifies the Chitose dialectal cognate form for Saru aan"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--awan-expresses-surprise-at-unexpected-fact","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topics":["topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--mirativity-aan"],"statement":{"en":"The form a-(w)an (plural rok-okai) expresses surprise at an unexpected fact or result.","ja":"a-(w)an（複数形 rok-okai）は予期せぬ事実や結果に対する驚きを表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["a-wan","awan","rok-okai"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0198-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--aan-rokkoka-admirative-mood-auxiliaries","differs_in":null,"note":"Early description of the same singular/plural auxiliary pair expressing mirative surprise"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--anan-expresses-delayed-realization","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topics":["topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--mirativity-aan"],"statement":{"en":"The auxiliary verb anan expresses that a fact was not understood at the time but became clear and accepted later.","ja":"助動詞 anan は、その時点では分からなかった事実が後になって判明・納得されたことを表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["anan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0096-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0246-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--chitose-anan-corresponds-to-saru-aan","differs_in":null,"note":"Detailed semantics of the Chitose cognate anan as delayed realization"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--aan-denotes-mirativity-by-semantic-extension","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topics":["topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization","topic:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--mirativity-aan"],"statement":{"en":"The auxiliary verb aan denotes mirativity as an extension of its meaning.","ja":"助動詞 aan は意味の拡張として新奇性・驚異性（ミラティビティ）を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["aan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:yoshikawa2022@handbook-epub/l0128-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:evidential/mirativity-scope-grammaticalization--aan-rokkoka-admirative-mood-auxiliaries","differs_in":null,"note":"Characterizes the mirative function of aan as a semantic extension"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
